408,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":67.9,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.037143916533450075,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":52.4,"_gate_share_shrink":0.015296565790678285,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":30.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004882246739666459,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":91.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.00437,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.9,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Watsco, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, engages in the distribution of air conditioning, heating, and refrigeration equipment, and related parts and supplies in the United States, Canada, Latin America, and the Caribbean. It distributes equipment, including residential ducted and ductless air conditioners, such as gas, electric, and oil furnaces; commercial air conditioning and heating equipment systems; and other specialized equipment. The company also offers parts comprising replacement compressors, evaporator coils, motors, and other component parts; and supplies, such as thermostats, insulation materials, refrigerants, ductworks, grills, registers, sheet metals, tools, copper tubing, concrete pads, tapes, adhesives, and other ancillary supplies, as well as plumbing and bathroom remodeling supplies. It serves contractors and dealers that service the replacement and new construction markets for residential and light commercial central air conditioning, heating, and refrigeration systems. Watsco, Inc. was incorporated in 1956 and is headquartered in Miami, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Albert H. Nahmad | Chairman & CEO | Age 84 | Compensation: $833,620 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $1.0M ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $77K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Watsco, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $12.8B market cap on $7.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -0% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 30% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 20-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 25% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $535M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.15\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Carries a 35% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.348036253776435},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","33 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"24,844 Watsco, Inc. $WSO Shares Sold by King Luther Capital Management Corp","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/24844-watsco-inc-wso-shares-sold-by-king-luther-capital-management-corp.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794566476.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Watsco (NYSE:WSO) Reshaping the HVAC Map?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/midcap/is-watsco-nysewso-reshaping-the-hvac-map","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794404340.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Watsco (WSO) Undervalued As Earnings Reset Growth Expectations?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-wso/watsco/news/is-watsco-wso-undervalued-as-earnings-reset-growth-expectati","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794320546.195,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why (WSO) Price Action Is Critical for Tactical Trading","source":"news.stocktrader